From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: Lock screen: a pattern lock (de.yesman.neo lock-type)

With de.yesman.neo's lock-type set to 'pattern', the unlock page shows a 3x3
dot grid instead of the keypad, as on Android: the dots joined in order (a dot
passed over joins too) go to PAM as the password ("1478"), so the user's
password is the pattern. Fewer than 4 dots or a wrong pattern turn red for a
second. 'swipe' is Phosh's own require-unlock = false, set by Mobile Settings
alongside; 'pin' keeps the keypad.
---
--- a/src/lockscreen.c	2026-10-10 01:14:21.662404029 +0200
+++ b/src/lockscreen.c	2026-10-10 01:14:38.191676805 +0200
@@ -105,6 +105,17 @@
